#X text 200 440 <- change the activation of the whole layer, f 50;
#X text 200 480 Chain layers: connect the outlet (bang when done) of one [nn.dense] to the inlet of the next \, with the output array of the first as the input array of the second., f 60;
#X obj 680 100 cnv 1 410 520 empty empty REFERENCE 8 12 0 13 #eef1f5 #1d3557 0;
#X text 690 126 ARGUMENTS: 1) input array 2) output array 3) activation (default tanh)., f 56;
#X text 690 162 Weights: array <output>_w (n_out * n_in). Biases: array <output>_b (n_out). All array names must start with a letter and contain no "-" ([expr] reads them). Tip: x\$0_name gives a unique name per patch., f 56;
#X text 690 243 LEFT INLET: bang = compute \, a function name = change activation. OUTLET: bang when the output array is ready., f 56;
#X text 690 294 LOADING TRAINED WEIGHTS: arrays read text files with numbers separated by spaces: [ \, x1003_out_w read weights.txt(. See python/train_vae.py and lesson 11 \, where an autoencoder trained in Python runs live in Pd., f 56;
